### 1.1 Gym check-ins never reach `gym_check_ins` — [V: membership_session]
- Defect: `addMemberCheckIn` in `store.ts` updates local `memberCheckIns` and undo only; `memberService.recordCheckIn` is never called. `addWalkInTicket` does sync.
- Fix: call `memberService.recordCheckIn` through the offline queue; hydrate `memberCheckIns` from `gym_check_ins`; delta-sync cursor for the table.
- Edge cases: duplicate check-in within N minutes (configurable guard, default 5, with override by owner); expired/frozen/suspended member (block or warn per business setting, log override with staff ID); balance due; check-in at midnight boundary; RFID double scan; undo of check-in must delete the remote row; member deleted after check-in; offline then reconnect ordering.
- Also verify walk-in ticket numbering `WI-YYYY-XXXX` is unique under concurrency across devices (server-side sequence or device-prefixed counter) and that timbre is applied only when the business setting requires it.

### 1.2 Quick roll call local-only — [V: education_cohort]
- Defect: `AcademyRollCallKiosk` → `recordQuickAttendance` mutates `eduQuickAttendance` only.
- Fix: persist to `edu_attendance` using the same schema and conflict key as `RollCallModal` (session + student). Remove `eduQuickAttendance` as a parallel truth, or make it a derived view. Migrate any existing local records on first load.
- Edge cases: student not enrolled in the cohort; session already closed; re-marking a student (upsert, keep audit trail of changes); late arrival time; excused with reason; both kiosk and `RollCallModal` used for the same session (last-write-wins with audit, no duplicates); PIN gate via `PinVerificationModal` records who took attendance.

### 1.3 Salon chair board in local state — [V: appointment_service]
- Defect: `SalonQuickChairKiosk` keeps occupied-chair assignments in `useState`, bypassing `updateSalonChairStation` (`salon_chair_stations`).
- Fix: drive the board from store/synced `salon_chair_stations`; assignment, timer start (store `started_at`, compute elapsed from timestamp, never from an in-memory counter), completion, and checkout all write through the store.
- Edge cases: page reload mid-service restores timer; two devices assign the same chair (conflict resolution); appointment cancelled while in chair; stylist double-booked; chair out of service; checkout with split payment; walk-in without client record.

### 1.4 POS cash drawer, opening float, petty cash, Z-report volatile — [V: pos_inventory]
- Defect: `PosFinanceView` holds `expenses`, `openingFloat` (15000 default), `actualCashInput` in component state; lost on reload.
