## 6. PHASE 2 — SHARED HORIZONTAL FOUNDATIONS [ALL]

Build these as shared modules once, then adopt them per vertical. Each module needs its own schema, service, hooks, UI primitives, tests, and a migration plan. Do not create per-vertical copies.

### 6.1 Unified document and invoicing engine
- One engine for: quote (devis), order, delivery note, invoice, credit note (avoir), receipt, proforma.
- Requirements: gap-free legal numbering per business, per document type, per fiscal year (allocated server-side via RPC to survive offline devices: use per-device reserved ranges or deferred final numbering with draft IDs); TVA per line (0/9/19 via statutory config); Timbre Fiscal (Art. 317 helper reused everywhere, one implementation); retenue de garantie; discounts; rounding rule; total in words (FR/AR, reuse `algerianPtt`); NIF/NIS/RC/AI header from the fiscal profile with graceful missing-field handling; immutable once issued (changes via credit note); PDF/print template (A4, 80 mm) editable per business (logo, footer, language).
- Migrate `CommercialDocument` (trading) onto it first as the reference implementation, then adopt in: membership (fix 3.2), project_milestone (client invoicing), rental_booking, manufacturing (sales side), legal_accounting (fee invoices), education (tuition), garage, real_estate, agriculture, logistics (merchant fees), medical (invoices).
- Edge cases: invoice for a deleted customer; currency (DZD/EUR/USD for freelance with stored FX rate and date); partial payments; overpayment (credit balance); cancelled/voided invoices keep their number; duplicate issuance; clock skew between devices.

### 6.2 Unified payments ledger
- One `payments` table and service: method (cash, CCP, bank transfer, CIB, BaridiMob, cheque, traite, member balance, credit), amount, date, document reference, who recorded, cash session link.
- Cheques and traites (post-dated instruments): due date, bank, status (received, deposited, cleared, bounced); bounced cheque reopens the invoice balance. Primary need: trading, but build it shared.
- Adopt in all verticals; replace synthesized payment rows (e.g. `MembershipFinanceView`).
- Edge cases: allocation of one payment across multiple invoices; refund; payment reversal with audit; payment dated in a closed period (block); duplicate payment submission (idempotency key).

### 6.3 Shared accounting layer (SCF)
- Expand the legal-only SCF ledger into a shared double-entry engine (`journal_entries`, `journal_lines`, chart of accounts seeded with SCF, fiscal years, period locking).
- Every vertical posts via a posting-rules layer (sale, purchase, payment, payroll, stock movement, depreciation later). Entries must always balance (reuse `validateAndBalanceSCFEntry`); posting failures go to a retry queue and a visible "unposted" report, never silently dropped.
- Deliver: trial balance, general ledger, bank/cash reconciliation, TVA report ready for G50 preparation, and CSV/PDF exports. `[VERIFY]` the exact G50/TAP/IBS formats with an accountant before claiming compliance; label exports "preparation aid" until validated.
- Edge cases: reversal entries; multi-currency; period close/reopen with permission; backdated entries; imbalance rounding differences.

### 6.4 Unified CRM and communication
- One `party` master (person or company) linkable from member, client, patient, renter, student, B2B client, owner, merchant, etc., with duplicate detection (phone, NIF, email) and merge with audit.
- Customer 360 view: all documents, payments, appointments, tickets, notes, communications across verticals.
- Follow-up tasks and reminders; message templates (FR/AR/EN) for SMS/WhatsApp/email with variables; consent/opt-out flag respected everywhere; delivery log.
- Edge cases: phone normalization to +213 formats (`validateAlgerianPhone` reused); duplicate phones across parties (shared family phone); opt-out; template variable missing; provider failure → retry and surface status.

### 6.5 Reminder and notification engine
- Rule-based events: membership expiring, invoice overdue, installment due, rent due, appointment tomorrow, low stock, expiry date, service due (garage), DAR lockout, cheque due, deadline (CPCA), contract expiry, vehicle documents expiry. Channels: in-app, SMS/WhatsApp (when 6.4 is configured), email.
- Idempotent scheduling (a reminder is never sent twice), per-business quiet hours, per-rule enable/disable, delivery log.

### 6.6 Shared inventory/WMS services
- Extract a shared stock service from trading, POS, manufacturing, garage, agriculture, medical consumables: warehouses/bins, lots/batches with expiry (FEFO), serial numbers, stock counts (cycle count with variance posting), reorder rules (min/max → suggested purchase), unit conversions (piece/carton/pallet), barcode label printing, landed cost (freight, customs, FX) for import flows, consignment/returnable packaging ledger.
- Edge cases: negative stock policy (block/allow per business); concurrent consumption (atomic decrement via RPC); transfer in transit; lot recall; expired lot sale block; count during active sales.
- Adoption order: trading → POS → manufacturing → garage → agriculture → medical consumables.

### 6.7 CSV/Excel import
- Import wizard for: members, clients, patients, products, suppliers, staff, vehicles, parcels, properties, students. Steps: upload → column mapping (saved templates) → validation preview with row-level errors → dry run → commit in chunks with rollback on failure → import report download.
- Edge cases: encoding (UTF-8, Windows-1256, ISO-8859-1), delimiters (`,` `;`), Excel date serials, Arabic digits, phone formats, duplicates (skip/update/merge option), 50,000-row files, malformed rows, formula-injection strings, partial failure.

