## 12. TEST & CI REQUIREMENTS

### 12.1 Unit tests
All rule modules (`algerianPayroll`, `staffRules`, `realEstateRules`, `manufacturingRules`, `legalRules`, `logisticsRules`, `contractorRules`, `agriRules`, `algerianPtt`, timbre helpers): boundary values, rounding, and every statutory bracket.

### 12.2 Integration tests
Per vertical: create → edit → status transition → delete → undo → offline → reconnect → verify remote rows. Sync tests: queue replay twice (idempotent), conflict 409 path, poison mutation quarantine.

### 12.3 Role-access matrix test
Auto-generate from the permission definition: for every vertical × role × route, assert allowed component or explicit denial. Fail CI when Sidebar and App.tsx disagree.

### 12.4 End-to-end tests (Playwright)
One golden path per vertical (e.g. gym check-in offline → sync; POS sale → refund → Z-report; trading devis → facture → payment; legal escrow release; logistics parcel → manifest → discharge; payroll run → payslip print).

### 12.5 CI guards
- Fail on `showToast` calls in handlers that contain no store/service call (lint rule or script).
- Fail on forbidden literals (`acc_01`, hardcoded NIFs, `unsplash.com`, `supabase.co` project refs, `58 WILAYAS`) outside fixtures.
- Fail on new hardcoded user-facing strings (i18n check).
- Fail on new `localStorage.setItem` keys not registered in a central key registry with an owner and purpose.
- Type-check, lint, unit, integration, e2e must pass before merge.

